course: dictionary
lesson: 15438
title: Stead: a word that lives in phrases
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Stead» is an old word, and you will rarely meet it on its own. You will find it in set phrases, which are groups of words that always go together. When you meet a phrase, read the whole phrase, not just one word at a time.
explain: «Ella was ill, so her brother played in her stead.» In her stead means in her place, instead of her. Try it: put «in her place» into the sentence. Brother played in her place, so the meaning fits.
explain: «Practising your times tables will stand you in good stead.» To stand someone in good stead means to be useful to them later on. The clue is the word «later»: the practice helps you in the future, not just today.
fact: A phrase is a group of words that often goes together and has its own meaning.
fact: «In someone's stead» means in their place, instead of them.
fact: «Stand you in good stead» means it will be useful to you later.
fact: «Instead» is made from «in» and «stead», and it still carries the meaning of "in place of".
fact: Long ago, «stead» meant a place or a farm, and it still lives on in words like «homestead».
exercise: «Ella was ill, so her brother played in her stead.» What does in her stead mean? | Next to her on the bench | *In her place, instead of her | Before she got better | Without any shoes on
exercise: «Practising your times tables will stand you in good stead.» What does stand you in good stead mean? | *It will be very useful to you later | It will make you tired now | It will be finished by lunchtime | It will hurt your feet
exercise: Which two smaller words make up instead? | is and tead | in and stood | in and head | *in and stead
test: Homestead comes from an old word for stead. What did stead once mean? | A river | *A place or a farm | Hungry | A kind of boat
test: «Grandma could not come, so Dad went in her stead.» Who went? | *Dad | Nobody | Both of them | Grandma
exam: «Reading every day will stand you in good stead when you take your exams.» What does this mean? | It will finish quickly | It will be boring | *It will help you later | It will cause trouble
